  "verse_id": "tsa-a21-v04",
  "song": "tsa-a21",
  "verse": 4,
  "quick_english": "Some are established in Veda-tradition-and-rest scriptures, in the self of Māyā-fitting-difference-contemplation; others just that kind by liberation-claim, in Sāṃkhya-Vaiṣṇava-scriptures-and-rest; others in the essence of reflecting separated Śiva-nature, in Śaiva-Siddhānta-and-rest; others in the essence of reflecting all-pervasive Lordhood, in Maṅgala-and-rest scriptures; but some very rare, in the self reflecting the Lord's own nature bound by exhaustive limitation-free-bliss-supreme-truth-made-of-consciousness, in the order of blessed Trika scripture; but some by earlier-earlier-abandonment order or by transcendence — thus in this way one-fruit-attainment from one tradition alone.",
